        <hasRequirement rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R6"/>
        <hasRequirement rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R4"/>
        <hasRequirement rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R7"/>
        <hasRequirement rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R2"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R3 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R3">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R3_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseTime"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Time R3 - Occurrences of the phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns the occurrences of a phase - whether and when it existed in an experiment - to its time context. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: did the phase exist in this experiment, and when? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: its own occurrences (cpo:hasOccurrence). The series lays out every possible phase; the occurrence in an experiment says whether the phase existed there and when (rule 7c.1 of the crate rules). Status, start, end and duration hang on the occurrence and are reached from it. A phase that is always there - the room air, the content of a supply line - has no occurrence of its own: its permanent occurrence stands at its library entry and is assigned by Phase_Time_R4. Not here: the arrival of a container content in the lab is a different event at its library entry (Phase_Time_R1, R4); that an occurrence which occurred has its start, end and duration is checked by the data quality shape hlo:Phase_Occurrence_Times_Shape, since the generator creates those times itself. An assignment (rule 7.16): nothing is required, the shape never reports - the generator gives every phase of an experiment its occurrence.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R3_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R3_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R1 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R1">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R1_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseTime"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Time R1 - Arrival time of a container content</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">For every container content in use, its library entry records when it arrived in the lab.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: since when has this content been in the lab? Applies to: every Phase in use that is the content of a chemical container - its material is cpo:materialContainedIn a cpo:ChemicalContainer, a bottle, can or gas cylinder of the chemical inventory. Not to Fixed phases: they are the library entries themselves (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: up the chain of the phase (hlo:specializationOf), its library entry - the Fixed entry in the material library - has its arrival: an occurrence with a start time. The start says when the content came into the lab; it is the end of the task that delivered it (receiving) or made it in the lab (preparing, a reaction), and that task is assigned by Phase_Information_R5. The content of a chemical container always has such an entry, since it belongs to the container and not to an experiment (the class cpo:ChemicalContainer); the arrival stands once, at that entry, and every level reads it from there. Reports: the library entry has no arrival, or the arrival has no start time - once per level, at the content itself. Not here: whether and when the phase existed in an experiment is its own occurrence (Phase_Time_R3); where the material of every other phase comes from is checked by Phase_Time_R2, which does not apply to container contents and does not ask for times, so a missing arrival time is reported only here; the arrivals of everything a content may have come from - for a stock solution, the bottles it was made from - are assigned by Phase_Time_R4. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R1_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R1_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R5 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R5">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R5_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseTime"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Time R5 - Opening of the containers upstream</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns to the time context of a phase the opening time of every container on its way back. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: when were the containers opened that its material may have come from? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: the opening time (cpo:hasOpeningTime at the container, read through hlo:specializationOf) of the container its own material is in and of every container on its way back. The way back is the same in Phase_Time_R2 and R4-R6 and in Phase_Information_R4/R5: backwards over the transfers (cpo:addsToPhase inverted, then cpo:removesFromPhase) and up the chain (hlo:specializationOf), any number of steps in any order; zero steps is the phase itself. At a library entry it continues over the transfers of a preparation, so a stock solution reaches the bottles it was made from. Transfers are potential: these are all the containers the material may have come from - downstream of a reactor, in which substances move between the phases in both directions, every container upstream; per substance is not possible in SHACL Core. The time is linked; material and container lie on the way. Not here: when a content arrived in the lab (Phase_Time_R1, R4), its expiry (Phase_Time_R6), the containers themselves (Phase_Time_R7). Its counterpart for the molecule is Molecule_Time_R2: the same path and the same value shape, with one step in front (from the molecule up to its phase). An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports - a delivered container may still be closed, and one filled in the lab was never sealed.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R5_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R5_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R6 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R6">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R6_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseTime"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Time R6 - Expiry or re-test of the materials upstream</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns to the time context of a phase the expiry or re-test time of every material on its way back. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: when do the chemicals its material may have come from expire, or need to be tested again? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: the expiry or re-test time (cpo:hasExpiryTime or cpo:hasRetestTime - stated at the library entry of a content, which carries its lot, and read through hlo:specializationOf) of its own material and of every material on its way back. The way back is the one of Phase_Time_R5: backwards over the transfers and up the chain, any number of steps in any order, zero steps being the phase itself, at a library entry also over the transfers of a preparation. Transfers are potential, so these are all the materials it may have come from; per substance is not possible in SHACL Core. The time is linked; the material lies on the way. Not here: the lot itself (Phase_Information_R4 - the same way, so that the information context has the lots whose expiry the time context has); the opening of the containers (Phase_Time_R5). Its counterpart for the molecule is Molecule_Time_R3: the same path and the same value shape, with one step in front (from the molecule up to its phase). An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports - a stable substance has a re-test date instead of an expiry date, and some have neither.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R6_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R6_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R4 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R4">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R4_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseTime"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Time R4 - Arrivals upstream</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns to the time context of a phase the arrival of every content and supply its material may have come from. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: since when have the chemicals its material may have come from been in the lab? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: every arrival on its way back - the occurrence at the Fixed library entry of a container content, which starts when the content was delivered or made in the lab and ends when it was used up or disposed of - and the permanent occurrence of a supply that is always there (the room air, the content of a supply line). The way back is the one of Phase_Time_R5: backwards over the transfers and up the chain, any number of steps in any order, zero steps being the phase itself, at a library entry also over the transfers of a preparation - so a container content reaches its own arrival, and a stock solution also those of the bottles it was made from. Transfers are potential, so these are all the origins it may have come from; per substance is not possible in SHACL Core. The occurrence is linked; status, start and end are reached from it. Only occurrences at Fixed entries count: the occurrences of an experiment are filtered out (Phase_Time_R3). Not here: the arrival time of a container content is required at the content (Phase_Time_R1); that every other phase reaches at least one origin is checked by Phase_Time_R2 on the same way back - it checks that something is found, this assignment links everything found, for every phase; the tasks that delivered or made the contents are the information counterpart (Phase_Information_R5). Its counterpart for the molecule is Molecule_Time_R1: the same path and the same value shape, with one step in front (from the molecule up to its phase). An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R4_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R4_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R7 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R7">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R7_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseTime"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Time R7 - Containers upstream on the same level</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns to the time context of a phase every chemical container of its own level its material is in or may have come from. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: from which containers of this experiment can its material come? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: the chemical containers (cpo:ChemicalContainer) of its own level that its material is in or may have come from - backwards over the transfers of that level only (cpo:addsToPhase inverted, then cpo:removesFromPhase, any number of times; zero times is the phase itself), then to the material (dcterms:isPartOf) and its container (cpo:materialContainedIn). The container is linked; its use before this level (cpo:lastUsedTime, Device_Time_R1), its delivery and its opening are reached from it. Only the own level, unlike Phase_Time_R4-R6: the containers that stood in this experiment or series, with what holds for it - not their library entries, and not the bottles a stock solution was once made from, which never stood in the experiment. Other devices - a reactor, a vial - are filtered out: their context is the device, not the origin of a phase. Transfers are potential; per substance is not possible in SHACL Core. Not here: what is known about the origins along the whole way back - opening, expiry and arrival (Phase_Time_R4-R6). Its counterpart for the molecule is Molecule_Time_R4: the same path and the same value shape, with one step in front (from the molecule up to its phase). An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R7_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R7_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R2 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R2">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R2_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseTime"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Time R2 - Known origin of the material</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use outside a chemical container, except device bodies and the surroundings, can be traced back to at least one origin: a container content or a supply that is always there.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: can it be traced where the material of this phase came from? Applies to: every Phase in use outside a chemical container - in a reactor, a feed line, a stream between devices. Not to Fixed phases; not to the content of a chemical container, whose arrival Phase_Time_R1 asks for; not to the phases of a device body (cpo:BodyMaterial) or of an environment (cpo:Environment), whose material is not supplied (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: on its way back it reaches at least one origin - an occurrence at a Fixed library entry: the arrival of a container content, or the permanent occurrence of a supply that is always there (the room air, the content of a supply line). The way back is the one of Phase_Time_R5: backwards over the transfers and up the chain, any number of steps in any order, zero steps being the phase itself, at a library entry also over the transfers of a preparation. Every origin found is linked (the occurrence). Reports: the phase is fed only from an unnamed source outside the system (cpo:Source), or no transfer leads into it at all - a gap in the description of the process. Not here: the arrival time is required at the container content (Phase_Time_R1), so a missing one is reported once, there, and not again at every phase downstream; all arrivals on the way back are assigned to every phase, container contents included, by Phase_Time_R4 on the same way back - it links everything found, this requirement checks that something is found; which substance came from where cannot be determined in SHACL Core. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R2_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Time_R2_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R1 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R1">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R1_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseEnergy"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Energy R1 - Temperature</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use has an actual temperature.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: how warm is this phase? Applies to: every Phase in use. Not to Fixed phases: temperature is a per-use fact - the body material of a device in the library is at no temperature of its own (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: it has an Actual ProcessVariable for its temperature (cpo:hasTemperature, QuantityKind Temperature). Where a library entry carries one - the room air, at the assumed conditions of the lab - the phase's own temperature specializes it, and the collecting path reaches it along the chain (Info). Reports: no such Actual. Not here: the temperature of the material volume or stream around the phase (Phase_Energy_R6) and of the phases in contact (Phase_Energy_R8) are only collected; the wall temperature of a device is Device_Energy_R1. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R1_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R1_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R2 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R2">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R2_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseEnergy"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Energy R2 - Pressure</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use has an actual pressure.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: what pressure is this phase under? Applies to: every Phase in use. Not to Fixed phases: pressure is a per-use fact (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: it has an Actual ProcessVariable for its pressure (cpo:hasPressure, QuantityKind Pressure). Where a library entry carries one - the room air, at the assumed conditions of the lab - the phase's own pressure specializes it, and the collecting path reaches it along the chain (Info). Reports: no such Actual. Not here: the pressure of the material volume or stream around the phase (Phase_Energy_R7) and of the phases in contact (Phase_Energy_R9) are only collected; the wall pressure of a device is Device_Energy_R2. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R2_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R2_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R3 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R3">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R3_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseEnergy"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Energy R3 - Flow rate</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use that is part of a stream has an actual flow rate, recorded on the stream.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: how fast does the stream this phase is part of flow? Applies to: every Phase in use that is part of a Stream; phases that are not (e.g. in a static MaterialVolume) are not affected. Not to Fixed phases: a flow rate is a per-use fact, like temperature and pressure (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: its stream (dcterms:isPartOf) has an Actual ProcessVariable for its flow rate (cpo:hasFlowrate), its values given in one of the kinds cpo:valueHasQuantityKind allows (volume, molar or mass flow rate) - the flow rate is recorded only on the Stream, never duplicated onto the Phase. Reports: the stream has no such Actual - at each of its phases. Not here: the kinds of the values are checked on the values themselves (rule 4.4). An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R3_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R3_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R5 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R5">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#SurroundingsRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R5_ContextPathShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseEnergy"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Energy R5 - Energy fields around a phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Collects every energy field a phase is exposed to: those of whatever holds it (material volume or stream, device, ambient air, room, site) and of everything within its setup, the other phases of its material included. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: which energy fields act on this phase? Applies to: every Phase. Collects: every EnergyField it is exposed to. The path first climbs to whatever holds the phase - the MaterialRepresentation it is part of (its cpo:MaterialVolume - the content of a device, the body material of a device, the room air - or its cpo:Stream), the Device that contains that material or is made of it (cpo:isBodyMaterialOf), the ambient air of the same level, the Room and the Site - and then goes down from each of those, also into every device standing in the room and into what stands inside it (cpo:isLocationOf, set by the generator within the crate and on the same level only). So a liquid phase also collects the fields of the gas phase in the same vessel and of the rest of the set-up: every field in a room acts everywhere in it, however weak - how strongly is the value of the field, not a matter of structure. A phase of a stream that no device contains climbs over the ends of the stream (cpo:flowsFrom, cpo:flowsTo) to the ports it connects and their devices, and from there into the room. Each field comes with what is recorded on its higher levels. The same path as Device_Energy_R6 and Molecule_Energy_R2. Not here: the phase's own field is required by Phase_Energy_R4 - a phase does not normally create one. A surroundings requirement (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): Info only and no minimum count, and what it collects is not linked (rule 6.3).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R5_ContextPathShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R5_ContextPathShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R6 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R6">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#SurroundingsRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R6_ContextPathShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseEnergy"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Energy R6 - Temperature of the material volume or stream around a phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Collects the temperature of the material volume or stream a phase is part of - the state of the contents as a whole. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: what is the temperature of the contents as a whole that this phase is part of? Applies to: every Phase. Collects: the temperature of the MaterialRepresentation it is part of - its cpo:MaterialVolume (the content of a device, the body material of a device, the room air) or its cpo:Stream - on every level along the chain of the value (dcterms:isPartOf, then cpo:hasTemperature, then hlo:specializationOf). The temperature of a material is the state of the contents as a whole, where setpoints, controlled values and measurements that cannot be assigned to a single phase are recorded (a probe in a stirred vessel). For a material with a single phase every value is recorded at the phase and the material's temperature stays empty. Not here: the phase's own temperature, a different statement, is required by Phase_Energy_R1; the temperatures of the phases in contact are collected by Phase_Energy_R8. A surroundings requirement (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): Info only and no minimum count, and what it collects is not linked (rule 6.3).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R6_ContextPathShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R6_ContextPathShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R7 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R7">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#SurroundingsRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R7_ContextPathShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseEnergy"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Energy R7 - Pressure of the material volume or stream around a phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Collects the pressure of the material volume or stream a phase is part of - the state of the contents as a whole. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: what is the pressure of the contents as a whole that this phase is part of? Applies to: every Phase. Collects: the pressure of the MaterialRepresentation it is part of - its cpo:MaterialVolume (the content of a device, the body material of a device, the room air) or its cpo:Stream - on every level along the chain of the value (dcterms:isPartOf, then cpo:hasPressure, then hlo:specializationOf). The pressure of a material is the state of the contents as a whole, where setpoints, controlled values and measurements that cannot be assigned to a single phase are recorded (a probe in a stirred vessel). For a material with a single phase every value is recorded at the phase and the material's pressure stays empty. Not here: the phase's own pressure, a different statement, is required by Phase_Energy_R2; the pressures of the phases in contact are collected by Phase_Energy_R9. A surroundings requirement (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): Info only and no minimum count, and what it collects is not linked (rule 6.3).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R7_ContextPathShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R7_ContextPathShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R4 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R4">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R4_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseEnergy"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Energy R4 - Own energy field</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use that can create an energy field has its own energy field.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: does a phase that creates an energy field have its field? Applies to: every Phase in use that can create an energy field (cpo:canCreateEnergyField = true) - a permanent magnet, a ferrofluid, a charged powder, a plasma; all other phases are not affected. The flag stands once, where it is first said (rule 3.6 of the crate rules): at the library entry of a phase that comes from a library, otherwise at the series phase, where the generator writes the answer to the question whether the phase creates a field of its own; the experiments read it through hlo:specializationOf. That is what tells a deliberate absence from a forgotten one. Not to Fixed phases: a phase in the library describes a material in general and need not carry a field of its own; the phase in use, which reads the flag through the chain, must have one (rule 7.7). Checks: it has at least one field of its own (cpo:hasEnergyField); its fields on the higher levels are collected along the chain of the field (Info). Reports: the flag is set and the phase has no field. Not here: the fields the phase is exposed to are collected by Phase_Energy_R5. Same pattern as Device_Energy_R5 and Molecule_Energy_R1. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R4_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R4_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R8 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R8">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#SurroundingsRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R8_ContextPathShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseEnergy"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Energy R8 - Temperature of the phases in contact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Collects the temperature of every phase a phase is in contact with. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: how warm is what this phase touches? Applies to: every Phase. Collects: the temperatures of the phases it touches - the values coupled with its own temperature (cpo:hasTemperature, then hlo:isCoupledWith), on every level along the chain of the value. The generator couples the temperatures of the two phases of every phase pair interface, the wall of the device the phase sits in included. Deliberately not the full up-and-down path of the energy fields (Phase_Energy_R5), which would bring the temperature of everything in the set-up: what matters is what the phase is in contact with. Not here: the phase's own temperature is required by Phase_Energy_R1; the temperature of its material as a whole is collected by Phase_Energy_R6. A surroundings requirement (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): Info only and no minimum count, and what it collects is not linked (rule 6.3).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R8_ContextPathShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R8_ContextPathShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R9 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R9">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#SurroundingsRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R9_ContextPathShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseEnergy"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Energy R9 - Pressure of the phases in contact</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Collects the pressure of every phase a phase is in contact with. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: what pressure is what this phase touches under? Applies to: every Phase. Collects: the pressures of the phases it touches - the values coupled with its own pressure (cpo:hasPressure, then hlo:isCoupledWith), on every level along the chain of the value: those of the phases it shares a phase pair interface with, the wall of the device included. Built like Phase_Energy_R8. Not here: the phase's own pressure is required by Phase_Energy_R2; the pressure of its material as a whole is collected by Phase_Energy_R7. A surroundings requirement (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): Info only and no minimum count, and what it collects is not linked (rule 6.3).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R9_ContextPathShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Energy_R9_ContextPathShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R1 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R1">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R1_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseInformation"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Information R1 - Entropy</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use has an actual entropy.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: what is the entropy of this phase? Applies to: every Phase in use. Not to Fixed phases: entropy is a per-use fact (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: it has an Actual ProcessVariable for its entropy (cpo:hasEntropy, QuantityKind Entropy). Filed under Information, not Energy or Substance: entropy measures how many microstates correspond to the macroscopic state - the information content of the state. Reports: no such Actual. Not here: temperature and pressure of the state (Phase_Energy_R1, R2). An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R1_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R1_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R2 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R2">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R2_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseInformation"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Information R2 - Lot of the content of a container</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use that is the content of a chemical container can be traced to the lot number of that content.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: which lot is this content from? Applies to: every Phase in use that is the content of a chemical container - its material is cpo:materialContainedIn a cpo:ChemicalContainer. Not to Fixed phases (rule 7.7 of the crate rules) and not to the phases of other materials. Checks: it reaches the lot of that content - cpo:hasLotNumber at its material, read through hlo:specializationOf. For a bought substance this is the manufacturer's lot number, for a substance produced in the lab its own batch or sample number (for instance the short label of the sample in the electronic lab notebook (ELN)). The manufacturer is deliberately not required, the lot is enough. Reports: no lot is reached. Not here: a lot number is a text, checked but not linked (rule 6.4); the materials that carry the lots upstream are assigned by Phase_Information_R4; the arrival of the content is Phase_Time_R1. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R2_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R2_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R4 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R4">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R4_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseInformation"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Information R4 - Lots upstream</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns to the information context of a phase the material carrying the lot of every content its material may have come from. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: from which lots can the material of this phase come? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: the Fixed material that carries the lot (cpo:hasLotNumber) of its own content and of every content its material may have come from - on the way back - any number of steps, each one transfer back (cpo:addsToPhase inverted, then cpo:removesFromPhase) or one step up the chain (hlo:specializationOf), in any order, so the transfers of the library count as well (a content prepared in the lab from other bottles) -, then to the material (dcterms:isPartOf) and its Fixed library entry. The material is linked, not the lot: a lot number is a text. The same way as Phase_Time_R6 (expiry), so that the information context of a reactor phase has the lots of the bottles its time context has. Transfers are potential; per substance is not possible in SHACL Core. Not here: the lot of the own content is required by Phase_Information_R2. Its counterpart for the molecule is Molecule_Information_R5: the same path and the same value shape, with one step in front (from the molecule up to its phase). An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R4_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R4_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R5 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R5">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R5_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseInformation"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Information R5 - Origin tasks upstream</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns to the information context of a phase the task that delivered or produced every content its material may have come from. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: which tasks delivered or made what the material of this phase can come from? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: the Fixed task that delivered (receiving) or produced (preparing in the lab) its own content and every content its material may have come from: the way of Phase_Time_R4 to the arrival of the content (its occurrence at the Fixed library entry), then from its start time backwards over cpo:hasEndTime - the task ends at the instant at which the arrival starts (rule 7.17 of the crate rules). The task is linked, not the time. Information rather than time: the task says how and from where - who delivered or prepared it, and from which bottles. Only Fixed tasks count, which keeps out the tasks of an experiment that end when an occurrence of the experiment starts. Not here: the arrival itself, the time counterpart, is assigned by Phase_Time_R4. Its counterpart for the molecule is Molecule_Information_R6: the same path and the same value shape, with one step in front (from the molecule up to its phase). An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R5_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R5_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R3 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R3">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R3_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseInformation"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Information R3 - Library entry of a phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns the library entry of a phase to its information context. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: which library entry does this phase come from? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: its library entry - the Fixed phase it specializes (hlo:specializationOf, one or more steps). A phase that comes from a library has one - the room air (organization library), the body material of a device (device library), the content of a chemical container or of a supply line (material library); through it the phase reads what stands once at the entry (rule 3.6 of the crate rules). A phase that arises in the experiment - a process phase or the phase of a stream - has none. Only the library phase is assigned; its material and its values are reached from it. Not here: that the content of a container reaches its library entry is required through its arrival (Phase_Time_R1) and its lot (Phase_Information_R2); devices and molecules always come from a library, their entry is required by Device_Information_R1 and Molecule_Information_R1. An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R3_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Information_R3_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R1 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R1">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R1_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSpace"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Space R1 - Volume</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use has an actual volume.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: how much space does this phase take up? Applies to: every Phase in use - a process phase as well as a phase of a device body, even if the value of the latter is known only at the Fixed library entry. Not to Fixed phases: a library entry may carry a volume, and the phase in use reaches it through the chain, but it is not required there (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: it has its own Actual ProcessVariable for its volume (cpo:hasVolume, QuantityKind Volume) on its level; a value on another level does not count, what is known about the value is collected along the chain of the Actual (Info). Unlike for a device, the volume is attached directly to the phase, not to a form. Reports: no such Actual. Not here: the dimensions of the phase's form, whose outer volume is this same Actual (Phase_Space_R2). An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R1_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R1_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R3 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R3">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R3_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSpace"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Space R3 - Total interfacial area</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use with an interface has an actual total interfacial area.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: how large is the whole boundary of this phase? Applies to: every Phase in use that has an aggregating PhaseInterface (cpo:hasPhaseInterface); phases without any interface (a phase that touches nothing, such as a stream between devices) are not affected. Not to Fixed phases (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: its interface has an Actual ProcessVariable for its area (cpo:hasPhaseInterface, then cpo:hasArea, QuantityKind Area) - the total interfacial area of the phase. Reports: no such Actual. Not here: this aggregate area is independent of, and deliberately not checked against, the areas on the phase's individual pair interfaces (Phase_Space_R4); that the phases of one material border on each other is checked by the data quality shape hlo:Phase_SameMaterial_Interface_Shape; the interfaces themselves are assigned by Phase_Space_R6. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R3_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R3_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R4 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R4">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R4_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSpace"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Space R4 - Area between two phases</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use reaches an actual area for each interface it shares with a neighbouring phase.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: how large is the contact area with each neighbouring phase? Applies to: every Phase in use, for each PhasePairInterface it is separated by (cpo:isSeparatedByInterface - the contact area between exactly this pair of adjacent phases, cpo:separatesPhases). Not to Fixed phases (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: each such interface has an Actual ProcessVariable for its area (cpo:hasArea, QuantityKind Area). The requirement starts at the phase, its context object (rule 7.11); the interface is a stage on the way, only its area belongs to the space context. Reports: a pair interface without an area - at both phases of the pair. Not here: a phase without neighbours has no pair interface; that the phases of one material border on each other is checked by the data quality shape hlo:Phase_SameMaterial_Interface_Shape; the total interfacial area is Phase_Space_R3, independent of this one. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R4_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R4_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_CuboidShape"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_SolidCylinderShape"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_SphericalShape"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_AnnulusShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSpace"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Space R2 - Dimensions of a phase form</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every form of a phase in use has the dimensions its class needs.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: how large is each form of this phase? Applies to: every Phase in use and the forms it defines (cpo:definesForm) - on the series and experiment level also the copies of the room form, which the room air defines since the room has no levels - on every level, directly. Not to Fixed phases: they define no form of their own (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). A phase that takes up exactly the region of something else (cpo:fillsForm: the solid phase of a device body) is checked there, under whatever defines that form. Checks: at each form the Actual ProcessVariables its class needs, as stated by the restrictions on the class in the ontology - the same classes as for devices (Device_Space_R1). A gas or liquid phase in a device takes the class of the device's cavity and shares its cross-section with it; its height, the fill level, is its own. The outer volume of the form is the volume of the phase (Phase_Space_R1), the same Actual. The requirement starts at the phase, its context object (rule 7.11): its forms are those it defines and those it fills where a phase or a material (the room air) defines them. A phase form is never hollow, so only the solid classes occur; a cpo:IndeterminateForm (a transferred portion, a dispersed phase) requires nothing. Reports: a missing dimension - the report names the phase, not which form or dimension. Not here: the layers of a device wall are not phase forms - the device defines them (Device_Space_R1), the layer phases only fill them; the aspect ratios are Phase_Structure_R2, the form itself Phase_Structure_R1. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_CuboidShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_CuboidShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_SolidCylinderShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_SolidCylinderShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_SphericalShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_SphericalShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_AnnulusShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R2_AnnulusShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R5 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R5">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R5_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSpace"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Space R5 - Occupation extent</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use reaches an actual occupation extent for each occupation state on its interface.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: how much of the interface of this phase does each occupation state take up? Applies to: every Phase in use, for each OccupationState on its interface (cpo:hasPhaseInterface, then cpo:hasOccupationState). Not to Fixed phases (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: each state has an Actual ProcessVariable for its extent (cpo:hasOccupationExtent) - a covered area or a fraction; in which kind its values are given is checked on the values themselves (rule 4.4). The requirement starts at the phase, its context object (rule 7.11); the state is a stage on the way. Reports: a state without an extent. Not here: the state itself belongs to the substance context (Phase_Substance_R6), only its extent to the space context. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R5_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R5_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R6 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R6">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R6_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSpace"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Space R6 - Interfaces of a phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns the interfaces of a phase to its space context. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: which interfaces does this phase have? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: its own PhaseInterface (cpo:hasPhaseInterface - the whole boundary of the phase, which carries its total interfacial area and its occupation states) and every PhasePairInterface it is separated by (cpo:isSeparatedByInterface - the contact with exactly one neighbouring phase: another phase of its material, the wall of its device, the room air). Not here: their areas are required by Phase_Space_R3 and R4, the occupation extents by Phase_Space_R5; that the phases of one material border on each other is checked by the data quality shape hlo:Phase_SameMaterial_Interface_Shape, since the generator builds those interfaces itself. An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports. A phase need not touch anything (a stream between devices).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R6_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Space_R6_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R1 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R1">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R1_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseStructure"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Structure R1 - Form</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use has a form: its own, or the one of the region it fills.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: which region of space does this phase take up? Applies to: every Phase in use, on every level, directly (rule 1 of the shapes). Not to Fixed phases (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: the phase has a form - the form of the region it takes up. A form describes a region of space, not a thing, and belongs to whatever sets the boundary of that region (cpo:definesForm); everything else that takes up exactly the same region points at the same form (cpo:fillsForm). So a phase has its own form where it sets the boundary itself - a continuous gas or liquid phase in a device, which shares the cross-section of the device's cavity and has its own fill level, or a phase whose class was asked for - and fills the form of its material where it takes up exactly the material's region: the only phase of a device body fills the form of the device, the room air phase the form of the room. A material with several such phases, or a phase whose shape cannot be given (a transferred portion), defines a cpo:IndeterminateForm - a statement, not a gap. So does a phase dispersed in another phase of its material (bubbles, particles): it has no single region, its size distribution (Phase_Structure_R4) describes it; alone in its material a dispersed phase fills the material's form. Reports: no form. Not here: the dimensions of a form are checked once, by the requirement of its class under whatever defines it (Phase_Space_R2 for a phase, Device_Space_R1 for a device); its aspect ratios by Phase_Structure_R2. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R1_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R1_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R4 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R4">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R4_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseStructure"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Structure R4 - Size distribution</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every dispersed phase in use has an actual size distribution of its bubbles, droplets or particles.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: how large are the bubbles, droplets or particles of a dispersed phase? Applies to: every Phase in use that is dispersed (cpo:hasDispersionState = Dispersed, read through hlo:specializationOf, since the dispersion state is a term recorded once and not repeated on every level); non-dispersed phases are not affected. Not to Fixed phases (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: it has its own Actual ProcessVariable for cpo:hasDispersedPhaseSizeDistribution or one of its subproperties (cpo:hasBubbleSizeDistribution, cpo:hasDropletSizeDistribution, cpo:hasParticleSizeDistribution) with QuantityKind Diameter, on every level. Reports: a dispersed phase without such an Actual. Not here: a phase dispersed in another phase of its material defines a cpo:IndeterminateForm (Phase_Structure_R1) - its size distribution describes it instead. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R4_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R4_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R3 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R3">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R3_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseStructure"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Structure R3 - Aggregate state</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use is typed as a gas, liquid or solid phase.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: is this phase a gas, a liquid or a solid? Applies to: every Phase in use. Not to Fixed phases (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: it is typed as cpo:GasPhase, cpo:LiquidPhase or cpo:SolidPhase (rdf:type), not just cpo:Phase - the aggregate state is deliberately modelled as the phase's own class, not as a separate property. Reports: a phase typed only as cpo:Phase. Not here: whether it is dispersed and how large its particles are (Phase_Structure_R4); the internal structure of a solid phase (Phase_Structure_R5). An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R3_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R3_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2_CuboidShape"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2_SolidCylinderShape"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2_AnnulusShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseStructure"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Structure R2 - Aspect ratios of a phase form</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every form of a phase in use has the aspect ratios its class needs.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: what proportions does each form of this phase have? Applies to: every Phase in use and the forms it defines (cpo:definesForm) - on the series and experiment level also the copies of the room form, which the room air defines since the room has no levels - on every level, directly. Not to Fixed phases: they define no form of their own (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). A phase that takes up exactly the region of something else (cpo:fillsForm: the solid phase of a device body) is checked there, under whatever defines that form. Checks: at each form the Actual ProcessVariables for the aspect ratios its class needs (subproperties of cpo:hasAspectRatio), as for devices (Device_Structure_R3). The requirement starts at the phase, its context object (rule 7.11): its forms are those it defines and those it fills where a phase or a material (the room air) defines them. A phase form is never hollow, so only the solid classes occur; a cpo:IndeterminateForm (a transferred portion, a dispersed phase) requires nothing. Reports: a missing ratio - the report names the phase, not which form or ratio. Not here: the dimensions (Phase_Space_R2), the form itself (Phase_Structure_R1). An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2_CuboidShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2_CuboidShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2_SolidCylinderShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2_SolidCylinderShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2_AnnulusShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R2_AnnulusShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R5 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R5">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R5_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseStructure"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Structure R5 - Internal structure of a solid phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every solid phase in use has an internal structure - crystalline, amorphous or semi-crystalline.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: is this solid crystalline, amorphous or semi-crystalline? Applies to: every SolidPhase in use, dispersed solid phases too - the particles of a powder have a structure. Not to Fixed phases (rule 7.7 of the crate rules): the phase in use reads the structure of its library entry through the chain, so a gap there is reported at the phase in use. Checks: it reaches an internal structure (cpo:hasSolidStructure: cpo:Crystalline, cpo:Amorphous or cpo:SemiCrystalline), a term read through hlo:specializationOf (rule 2 of the shapes): asked once for a process phase, recorded in the device library for the body material of a device (glass amorphous, stainless steel crystalline, polypropylene semi-crystalline). Reports: no structure is reached. Not here: the aggregate state (Phase_Structure_R3). An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R5_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Structure_R5_MainShape"/>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R1 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R1">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R1_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSubstance"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Substance R1 - Chemical constituents</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use contains at least one chemical entity.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: which chemical species does this phase consist of? Applies to: every Phase in use. Not to Fixed phases (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: it is linked via dcterms:hasPart to at least one ChemicalEntity. For a chebi:Molecule, dcterms:hasPart points to the phase-specific molecule record, not to the Fixed library entry - that record carries this phase's own concentration, mass, amount of substance and partial molar volume. The constituents are collected along the chain of the molecule records up to the library entries (Info). Reports: a phase without constituents. Not here: the concentration, mass and amount of substance of each molecule are assigned to the phase by Phase_Substance_R4 and required at the molecule (Molecule_Space_R2-R4); that a molecule stands in exactly one phase is Molecule_Space_R1. An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R1_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R1_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R4 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R4">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R4_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSubstance"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Substance R4 - Quantities of its molecules</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns the concentration, mass and amount of substance of each molecule of a phase to its substance context. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: what is the phase made of, and how much of each? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: for each molecule it consists of (dcterms:hasPart) its concentration, the mass of its substance in the phase and its amount of substance (cpo:hasConcentration, cpo:hasMass, cpo:hasAmountOfSubstance) - the composition of a phase, relative and absolute, is its substance context. The values stand once, on the per-phase molecule record, and are never duplicated onto the Phase; in a pure phase the mass of the molecule is the Actual of the phase's own mass (Phase_Substance_R2). In which kind a concentration is given is checked on the values themselves (the quantity kind shapes, rule 4.4 of the crate rules). Not here: the molecules themselves are linked by Phase_Substance_R1; each of the three quantities is required at the molecule (Molecule_Space_R2-R4), so a missing one is reported once, there; the partial molar volume of a molecule says how much space it takes up, not how much of it there is, and stays in the space context of the molecule (Molecule_Space_R5). An assignment (rule 7.16): nothing is required, the shape never reports.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R4_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R4_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R2 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R2">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R2_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSubstance"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Substance R2 - Mass</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use has an actual mass.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: what mass does this phase have? Applies to: every Phase in use. Not to Fixed phases: mass is a per-use fact (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: it has an Actual ProcessVariable for its mass (cpo:hasMass, QuantityKind Mass). Filed under Substance, not Energy: mass says nothing about the energetic state of the phase, only about the amount of substance present. In a pure phase it is the very Actual of the mass of its one molecule (Molecule_Space_R3). Reports: no such Actual. Not here: the density (Phase_Substance_R3); the masses of the molecules of a mixture are assigned by Phase_Substance_R4; the mass of a device body is the one of its phase (Device_Substance_R2). An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R2_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R2_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R3 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R3">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ExistenceRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R3_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSubstance"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Substance R3 - Density</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Every phase in use has an actual density.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: how dense is this phase? Applies to: every Phase in use. Not to Fixed phases: density is a per-use fact (rule 7.7 of the crate rules). Checks: it has an Actual ProcessVariable for its density (cpo:hasDensity, QuantityKind Density). Where a library entry carries one - the body material of a device, the room air - the phase's own density specializes it, and the collecting path reaches it along the chain (Info). Reports: no such Actual. Not here: the mass (Phase_Substance_R2); the density of a device body is the one of its phase (Device_Substance_R3). An existence requirement (rule 7.16).</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R3_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R3_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R5 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R5">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R5_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSubstance"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Substance R5 - Transfers of the phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns the transfers into or out of a phase to its substance context. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: what is carried into or out of this phase? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: the transfers into or out of it (cpo:addsToPhase, cpo:removesFromPhase): a transfer says whether, when and what is carried into or out of the phase. Its flow rate, transferred volume and occurrences are reached from the transfer and are not assigned themselves. Not here: the reactions of the phase (Phase_Substance_R7). An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports. A phase need not have transfers.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R5_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R5_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R6 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R6">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R6_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSubstance"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Substance R6 - Occupation states</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns the occupation states on the interface of a phase to its substance context. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: what is bound at the interface of this phase? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: the occupation states on its interface (cpo:hasPhaseInterface, then cpo:hasOccupationState): they say what the phase consists of at its interface, free or bound sites. Not here: how much of the interface each state takes up is required on the state (Phase_Space_R5). An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports. An interface need not have occupation states.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R6_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R6_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R7 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R7">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R7_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSubstance"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Substance R7 - Reactions of the phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns the reactions in a phase or at its interfaces to its substance context. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: which reactions take place in this phase or at its interfaces? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: its reactions - in it (cpo:occursInPhase) or at one of its interfaces (cpo:isSeparatedByInterface or cpo:hasPhaseInterface, then cpo:occursAtInterface); only values of class cpo:Reaction count, the transfers at the same interfaces do not. The rate, the occurrences and the partial orders of the participants are reached from the reaction and are not assigned themselves (the partial order deliberately gets no context of its own). Not here: the transfers of the phase (Phase_Substance_R5). An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports. A phase need not have reactions.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R7_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R7_MainShape"/>
    

    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R8 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R8">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#AssignmentRequirement"/>
        <hasShape rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R8_MainShape"/>
        <requirementOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#PhaseSubstance"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Phase Substance R8 - Solvent of the phase</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Assigns the solvent or solvents of a phase to its substance context. Nothing is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Question: which of its species is the medium of the mixture? Applies to: every Phase. Assigns: its solvent or solvents (cpo:hasSolvent) - which of its own species acts as the medium of the mixture is part of what the phase consists of. The solvent is one of the phase's own species and is therefore already linked to this context through Phase_Substance_R1 (dcterms:hasPart): the assignment states that the solvent belongs here, it adds no second link. Not here: the species themselves (Phase_Substance_R1). An assignment (rule 7.16 of the crate rules): nothing is required, the shape never reports. A phase need not name a solvent, and the generator never infers one.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R8_MainShape -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Phase_Substance_R8_MainShape"/>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Planned -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Planned">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ReferenceType"/>
        <determinedByTaskClass rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/ChemicalProcessOntology#PlanningTask"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fixed before the experiment, no guarantee it was applied.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Set -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#Set">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#ReferenceType"/>
        <determinedByTaskClass rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/ChemicalProcessOntology#SettingTask"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Applied once to a device without feedback; deviations are not corrected.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#SpaceCategory -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/lf576/ontologies/2026/7/HigherLevelOntology#SpaceCategory">
